The network shows roads between towns. The loop leaves $B$ and returns to $B$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3.2,0);
\coordinate (C) at (3.2,2.8);
\coordinate (D) at (0,2.8);
\draw (A)--(B);
\draw (A) .. controls (1.0,0.75) and (2.2,0.75) .. (B);
\draw (A) .. controls (1.0,-0.75) and (2.2,-0.75) .. (B);
\draw (B)--(C);
\draw (C)--(D);
\draw (D)--(A);
\draw (A)--(C);
\draw (B) .. controls (4.5,-0.8) and (4.5,0.8) .. (B);
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below=12pt] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above left] at (D) {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) How many vertices and edges are there?
(b) Find the degree of each vertex.
(c) Find the sum of the degrees.
(d) Is there a direct road between $B$ and $D$?
(e) What do the vertices and edges represent?

